  "custom_logic_notes": "The Supervisor function selects SL/TP dynamically based on which subsystem fires. Mode 'pass' parameter controls signal routing: 1=basic CCI only (SL/TP=sl1/tp1), 2=sale perceptron overrides sell signals (SL/TP=sl2/tp2) else falls back to CCI, 3=buying perceptron overrides buy signals (SL/TP=sl3/tp3) else falls back to CCI, 4=both perceptrons active with general perceptron as tiebreaker (output3>0 and output2>0 => buy with sl3/tp3; output3<=0 and output1<0 => sell with sl2/tp2; else falls back to CCI with sl1/tp1). The perceptron is a single-neuron model computing weighted sum of close price differences across evenly-spaced lookback bars. Deviation is set to Spread*3 points on each trade.",
