  "backtest_data_needs": "M1",
  "python_conversion_notes": "Perceptron logic is straightforward linear algebra (weighted sum of price differences). CCI is available in most Python TA libraries. Key complexity is the Supervisor routing with 4 pass modes that dynamically change SL/TP. Must replicate the mode-switching behavior exactly. SL/TP are set in points (not pips), multiplied by Sym.Point() and added/subtracted from Ask/Bid. No digit adjustment needed since Sym.NormalizePrice is used. The new-bar guard uses CopyTime comparison. Position check uses Pos.Select(_Symbol) to ensure flat before entry.",
